DELIRIUM: definition per DSM-V-TR
1) Disturbance of consciousness (i.e. reduced ability to focus, sustain, or shift attention);
2) Additional disturbance in cognition (memory, orientation, language, visuospatial ability, or perception);
3) Change from baseline, develops over a short period of time (usually hours to days) & tends to fluctuate;
4) Not better explained by another neurocognitive disorder and does not occur in the context of severely reduced arousal/coma.
Complications: a/w mortality (JAMA 2010;304:433), institutionalization (Lancet 2014;383:911), cognition (NEJM 2012;367:30)
